WEBVTT

00:06:58.382 --> 00:07:00.124
Now if you think about it, that's not funny.

00:07:00.124 --> 00:07:03.024
No one's laughing. (Laughter)

00:07:03.024 --> 00:07:04.994
And yet, there it is, so you assume

00:07:04.994 --> 00:07:06.351
there's been some kind of hiccup.

00:07:06.351 --> 00:07:08.185
Then Susan says "lol, I know,"

00:07:08.185 --> 00:07:10.482
again more guffawing than we're used to

00:07:10.482 --> 00:07:13.712
when you're talking about these inconveniences.

00:07:13.712 --> 00:07:16.456
So Julie says, "I just sent you an email."

00:07:16.456 --> 00:07:18.007
Susan: "lol, I see it."

00:07:18.007 --> 00:07:21.625
Very funny people, if that's what LOL means.

00:07:21.625 --> 00:07:23.753
This Julie says, "So what's up?"

00:07:23.753 --> 00:07:26.395
Susan: "lol, I have to write a 10 page paper."

00:07:26.395 --> 00:07:28.709
She's not amused. Let's think about it.

00:07:28.709 --> 00:07:31.390
LOL is being used in a very particular way.